# Test: ze bgp decode reads a capture back and decodes every BGP message in it
# VALIDATES: spec-bgp-pcap-decode AC-8 and AC-18 -- the round trip. The fixture
# below is a capture ze wrote with internal/core/pcap, so this test proves the
# writer and the reader agree at the process level.
# Exercises: cmdDecode -> decodePcapInput -> pcap.Reassemble -> frameMessages -> decodeHexPacket
# The session is the peer's OPEN, this host's OPEN, then a KEEPALIVE each way.

tmpfs=session.pcap:encoding=base64:terminator=EOF_PCAP
1MOyoQIABAAAAAAAAAAAAP//AABlAAAAwGFWaQAAAABFAAAARQAAAEUAAEUAAEAAQAa2r8AAAgHA
AAICALMAswAAAAEAAAABUBj//ybaAAD/////////////////////AB0BBP3oAFoBAgMEAMFhVmkA
AAAARQAAAEUAAABFAABFAABAAEAGtq/AAAICwAACAQCzALMAAAABAAAAHlAY//8mvQAA////////
/////////////wAdAQT96ABaAQIDBADCYVZpAAAAADsAAAA7AAAARQAAOwAAQABABra5wAACAcAA
AgIAswCzAAAAHgAAAB5QGP//JgEAAP////////////////////8AEwTDYVZpAAAAADsAAAA7AAAA
RQAAOwAAQABABra5wAACAsAAAgEAswCzAAAAHgAAADFQGP//Je4AAP////////////////////8A
EwQ=
EOF_PCAP

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze bgp decode pcap session.pcap
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=KEEPALIVE
expect=stdout:contains=65000
expect=stdout:contains=192.0.2.1:179
expect=stdout:contains=192.0.2.2:179
